>>
endobj
380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (SST Makerspace exists to bridge the gap between academic learning and real-world innovation by providing a structured community for hands-on research, prototyping, and product-driven experimentation. We create an environment where students, faculty, and industry partners collaborate to solve practical problems, develop engineering depth, and translate ideas into functional, market-relevant hardware solutions. By emphasizing applied learning, teamwork, and entrepreneurial thinking over grade-centric outcomes, the Makerspace cultivates technical competence, research discipline, and innovation readiness. Importantly, SST Makerspace is being intentionally developed as a scalable and replicable model, serving as a template for how universities can build sustainable, industry-aligned hubs that drive meaningful research, innovation, and hardware entrepreneurship.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (Our community is driven by core values that prioritize learning by doing, entertainment, and team spirit. We believe in gaining skills relevant to future development while maintaining a focus on practical problem-solving. While our primary target audience includes engineering students, we welcome any university student in Nigeria interested in hardware, IoT, and robotics.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
