444 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (The Rope Runner Challenge is designed to inspire students to think creatively about how robots can move across suspended cables or ropes, a task that requires a careful balance of grip, stability, and efficiency. While the challenge may look simple at first glance, it reflects real engineering problems faced in industries today. Around the world, cable-based robotics are being developed to inspect power lines, maintain communication cables, and even deliver goods across difficult terrain. They are also used in rescue situations to transport supplies across rivers, ravines, or disaster zones where ground access is impossible.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (For Nigeria, this competition is especially relevant. As the nation continues to expand its infrastructure and energy networks, reliable inspection and maintenance of power lines and transmission cables is critical to keeping the economy running. At the same time, disasters such as flooding, which affect many communities each year, highlight the need for innovative solutions to move goods and provide aid across blocked or unsafe areas. Encouraging young engineers to explore cable-traversing robotics creates a space to imagine practical, low-cost solutions that can be deployed in real Nigerian contexts.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
