598 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (To succeed in this activity, each team must ensure that their robot can reliably capture images, correctly overlay the team tag, measure distance accurately, and communicate with the server without corruption. A valid entry requires that the victim fills enough of the frame to be recognisable, the team information matches across both the image and metadata, and the robot maintains logical forward progression in its recorded distances. Lighting may vary slightly across the venue, so teams should avoid relying on auto-exposure alone and consider adding soft downward LEDs for stability. Image compression should be balanced: too high causes blur, too low results in long upload times. Teams should thoroughly test their JSON formatting, and encoder calibration before competition day.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
