856 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (System Architecture Overview - Mechanical, Electrical, Software)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
857 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (The Rope Runner bot operates as a unified, feedback-driven system where mechanical, electrical, and software subsystems function in a tight loop to navigate the 8-meter suspended track. The architecture begins with the mechanical subsystem, designed as an inverted walker that hangs from the rope to maintain a low center of gravity for passive stability. The chassis, fabricated from lightweight materials like 3D-printed PLA, is engineered to stay within a 30 cm cubed volume and support a 1kg payload while keeping the total weight under 2.5kg. Unlike traditional rolling robots, this system relies on specific "crawler arms" driven by DC motors to perform a grip-and-pull motion, enabling it to traverse the rope without utilizing wheels for linear movement.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
858 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (Powering this physical structure is the electrical subsystem, which serves as the robot's nervous system. A rechargeable LiPo battery, typically 7.4V, provides the necessary energy, splitting into two distinct power rails: a high-current path feeding an L298N H-bridge driver to actuate the motors, and a regulated logic rail powering the microcontroller, such as an ESP32 or Raspberry Pi. This central processing unit serves as the brain, integrating sensory inputs from a bottom-facing camera and a wheel encoder to create a digital understanding of the environment below the rope.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
859 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (The software subsystem acts as the orchestrator, running concurrent logic threads to manage both locomotion and mission-critical objectives. During the "Swiftplay" phase, the code focuses on motor synchronization and speed control via PWM signals to navigate obstructions like knots and vibrations. In the "Search and Rescue" phase, the software shifts to an intelligent surveillance role, fusing visual data from the camera with location coordinates from the encoder to identify, tag, and transmit images of "victims" to a local server using Wi-Fi. Seamless system integration is achieved when the software processes these sensory inputs in real-time to adjust mechanical torque and speed, ensuring the bot remains stable and responsive while executing complex data transmission tasks without pausing its journey.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
860 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (Note that these guidelines are just a way to help you get started with building your bot and are not the exact way every bot must be builts)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
