982 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Q: Can students from other universities participate in this category? )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
983 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (A: Yes. Unlike the Product Category, the Rope Runner Challenge is open to all active students of universities/colleges in Nigeria. You do not need to be a PAU student to compete in this category.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
984 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Q: Can we use wheels to drive along the rope? )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
985 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (A: No. The rules explicitly state that the robot must be an "inverted walker" that hangs from the rope. Wheels cannot roll along the top of the rope like a vehicle; the mechanism must "grip, clamp, or crawl.")
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
986 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Q: Is there a maximum weight limit? )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
987 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (A: There is no fixed numeric weight limit, but there is a performance limit. The robot must not cause noticeable rope sagging or deform/fray the rope. If your robot is too heavy and sags the line significantly during inspection, it may be disqualified.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
988 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Q: What happens if our robot falls off the rope? )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
989 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (A: You are allowed to pick it up. The "Fall Rule" states that you can manually retrieve the bot and reattach it at the last checkpoint successfully passed.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
990 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Important: The clock does not stop during this recovery. A fall essentially acts as a time penalty because you lose seconds resetting.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
991 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Q: What if our battery dies or a motor breaks during a run?)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
992 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (A: You may be granted a 5-minute retry window to fix the issue and restart, but this is at the judges' discretion and is reserved for genuine mechanical/electrical failures, not code errors.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
993 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Q: How do we qualify for the main event? )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
994 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (A: Registration alone does not guarantee a spot. You must submit a Video Entry demonstrating your robot successfully hanging from and traversing a rope. Only the top 10 teams from this video screening will be invited to the final competition.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
