/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (Frequently Asked Questions)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (Q: Can we apply with a team of fewer or more than five people? )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (A: No. The documentation specifies that interested participants must form teams of exactly five \(5\) students. This fixed number ensures that teams have the capacity to handle the workload \(technical, documentation, and business\) without being unwieldy.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (Q: Do we need to have a working prototype to apply? )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (A: No. At the application stage, you are not expected to build anything. The selection process is "purely cerebral," evaluating your problem understanding, structured thinking, and solution design rather than your manufacturing skills.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (Q: Can we work on our own startup idea instead of the provided problem? )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (A: No. This category is "Demand-Driven." All applicants must respond to a common problem statement provided by the SST Makerspace and its partners. This ensures you are solving a verified real-world problem for an SME rather than a hypothetical one.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (Q: Who pays for the materials to build the product? )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (A: The program structure implies that the SST Makerspace covers the development costs. This is evidenced by the rule stating that any team that fails to complete the build "will have to refund the full amount spent back to the organizing team." This suggests the organizers provide the initial funding or materials, which becomes a liability only if you drop out.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (Q: Can we skip the workshops if we already know the topic? )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (A: No. The four workshops \(Fabrication, Electrical, EDC Business, and Soft Skills\) are mandatory parts of the "Mentored Development Phase." Attendance and engagement in these sessions are tracked and contribute to the "Process" component of your final score.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (Q: What if our prototype breaks on Exhibition Day? )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 339 0 R
/E (A: You must pass a Pre-Exhibition Technical Review 2-3 weeks before the event to even qualify for the exhibition. This review checks for functionality and safety. If your product is a "non-functional concept" \(Vaporware\) at that stage, you will be barred from exhibiting.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
